 ## Overview
 Voxel Operations and Tests provide the fundamental mechanisms for querying, modifying, and combining discrete volumetric data structures after they have been generated [G]. While parent methods like [Voxelization](12-voxelization.md) focus on mapping continuous sources into a grid, this family addresses how to interact with that grid: checking spatial containment, transferring data blocks, and performing boolean or arithmetic logic on voxel values [G]. This family is distinct from generation techniques as it operates on the resulting data structure, enabling tasks such as collision detection, multi-field visualization, and volume editing [G].
